@startuml rwlock-lock-lifecycle
' RwLock guard lifecycle for the shared registries; poison recovery keeps them usable.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam state {
  ArrowColor #34495E
  BorderColor #34495E
  FontColor #2C3E50
}
title RwLock guard lifecycle — poison recovery keeps registries usable

state "Unlocked" as U #D6EAF8
state "ReadLocked(n)\nn concurrent readers (shared)" as RL #D6EAF8
state "WriteLocked\nexactly one writer (exclusive)" as WL #D6EAF8
state "Poisoned\na thread panicked while a guard was held" as P #E74C3C

[*] --> U
U --> RL : read()  (first reader)
RL --> RL : read() / drop  (n readers)
RL --> U : last reader drops
U --> WL : write()  (exclusive)
WL --> U : drop write guard
RL --> P : panic while held
WL --> P : panic while held
P --> U : read_lock / write_lock\nPoisonError::into_inner()  (recover)

note bottom of P
  duallity's read_lock / write_lock (src/lib.rs) recover the guard via
  into_inner() instead of re-panicking, so lazy expansion continues.
  Pinned by test_lock_helpers_recover_poisoned_lock.
end note
@enduml
